// source/boot/uefi/main.omg
//
// MILESTONE 1 — an Omega UEFI application that prints "Hello from Omega" through
// the firmware's Simple Text Output protocol and returns Success. BOOT-VERIFIED
// under QEMU/OVMF (2026-07-04): the serial console shows the greeting and the
// image returns Success. No C, no host runtime, no hand-written assembly — the
// whole stack is Omega plus the compiler's derivers. Aligned to the canonical
// compiling reference, Omega samples/uefi_hello (ea51376cd).
//
// The chain, all here + build.omg + the uefi contracts:
//   * build.omg sets efi_application + freestanding → an import-free PE32+ that
//     firmware loads directly.
//   * `boundary machine Main::run` is the EXPORTED CALLABLE: firmware calls it,
//     and the parameter list is the boundary-trusted shape over the registers it
//     hands us (handle in RCX, the SystemTable pointer in RDX). The boundary
//     VOUCHES transitively for `table`'s declared layout — no cast, no mint, in
//     trusted boot code.
//   * `table.con_out` projects the live SystemTable at the plan offset (+64) —
//     a dereference of the firmware pointer the boundary vouched for.
//   * `output_string -> output_string` (field model) dispatches through the protocol's own
//     vtable (mov rax,[rcx+8]; call rax) — COM/UEFI per-object dispatch.
//   * utf16"..." is the CHAR16 text UEFI expects.
//
// Typed-ABI note: Cathedral names the boot ABI with typed wrappers (EfiStatus,
// EfiHandle, &TextOutputProtocol) where the single-file sample used raw `addr`/`i32`.
// The typed form is the target as the toolchain threads typed params through the
// vtable path; the sample is the proven-compiling shape.

use uefi::uefi;            // EfiHandle, EfiStatus, EFI_SUCCESS, EfiSystemTable, TextOutputProtocol, SimpleTextOutput
use uefi::boot_services;   // BootServices
use own_machine;           // Main::own_machine (milestone 2, sibling module)
use omega::language::core::assembly; // PortIo, MachineControl

// Main's STATIC DATA (`&self`): the held capabilities (Simple Text Output for
// the greeting, Boot Services for the milestone-2 memory-map dance) + the
// greeting bytes + the memory-map buffer. The launch inputs (handle, table) are
// PARAMETERS to run, not fields of self — self is what the component IS, the args
// are what firmware handed this invocation.
data Main {
    out:      SimpleTextOutput;
    boot_svc: BootServices;      // milestone 2 — GetMemoryMap / ExitBootServices
    msg:      [u16; 19];         // "Hello from Omega\r\n\0" as UTF-16 CHAR16 code units
    map_buf:  [u8; 16384];       // static buffer for GetMemoryMap (no allocator yet)
}

// The firmware entry: an exported callable. `handle` is unused at milestone 1
// (milestone 2 needs it for ExitBootServices). The audited machine-state axioms
// (long mode, paging, interrupts, stack) are boot-target properties surfaced by
// the artifact — see the uefi contracts.
boundary machine Main::run(&self, handle: EfiHandle, table: &EfiSystemTable) -> EfiStatus
effects SimpleTextOutput + BootServices + PortIo + MachineControl
{
    self.msg = utf16"Hello from Omega\r\n\0";
    // Project con_out through a frame local (the reference-param deref), then
    // dispatch OutputString(con_out, &msg) through the firmware's own vtable.
    // No `validate` on the boot path — the boundary vouched for `table`'s shape.
    let con_out: &TextOutputProtocol = table.con_out;
    _ = self.out.output_string(con_out, &self.msg);
    // Milestone 2 — own the machine (own_machine.omg): walk the memory map, exit
    // boot services, mint the first Extent, then idle. Does NOT return (firmware
    // is gone after exit), so the terminal below is unreachable.
    self.own_machine(handle, table);
    transition { _ -> (EFI_SUCCESS) }
}
